SUMMARY:The Artist’s Voice: Tony Oursler with Susan Goldberg\, Meghan Cla
 re Considine\, and Nora Burnett Abrams
LOCATION:ICA\, 25 Harbor Shore Dr\, Boston\, MA 02210
DESCRIPTION:What does access to art look like? Today\, anyone with an inter
 net connection can explore art from around the world in seconds. But long 
 before streaming and social media transformed how we can experience cultur
 e\, a collaboration in Boston was already imagining a new way to bring con
 temporary art into people’s homes.\nhttps://www.icaboston.org/events/the
 -artists-voice-tony-oursler-with-susan-goldberg-meghan-clare-considine-and
 -nora-burnett-abrams/\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://www.icaboston.org/events/the-artists-voice-tony-oursler-with-su
 san-goldberg-meghan-clare-considine-and-nora-burnett-abrams/
END:VEVENT
